      "hints": [
        "For $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$, calculate $a = \\sin^2(\\pi/3) = \\frac{3}{4}$ and $d = -\\sin^4(\\pi/3) = -\\frac{9}{16}$.",
        "Apply $S_{16} = \\frac{16}{2}[2a + 15d]$ and evaluate."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate the first term $a$ and common difference $d$ at $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$ (noting $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$):\n$$a = \\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{3}{4}$$\n$$d = -\\sin^4\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^4 = -\\frac{9}{16}$$",
        "Apply the arithmetic series sum formula for $n = 16$ terms:\n$$S_{16} = \\frac{16}{2}[2a + 15d] = 8\\left[2\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) + 15\\left(-\\frac{9}{16}\\right)\\right]$$",
        "Evaluate the arithmetic expression:\n$$S_{16} = 8\\left[\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{135}{16}\\right] = 8\\left[\\frac{24 - 135}{16}\\right] = 8\\left[-\\frac{111}{16}\\right] = -\\frac{111}{2} = -55\\frac{1}{2} \\quad (\\text{or } -55.5)$$"
      ],
